  <h2>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Too many colours:</strong> Limit your active palette to 3-5 hues. More creates visual chaos.</li>
    <li><strong>Ignoring context:</strong> A bright palette works for a children's site but feels unprofessional for legal services.</li>
    <li><strong>Poor contrast:</strong> Light grey text on white is fashionable but unreadable.</li>
    <li><strong>Colour without meaning:</strong> Every colour choice should serve a purpose — decoration alone is not enough.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Conclusion</h2>

  <p>Colour theory is not about rigid rules — it is about understanding relationships so you can break them intentionally. Start with the wheel, learn the harmonies, respect accessibility, and always test in real contexts. The best palettes feel inevitable: every colour belongs exactly where it is.</p>

